course: dictionary
lesson: 9840
title: Swirl: moving round and round
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can do more than one job. «Swirl» can be an action word (a verb) or a thing (a noun). The words around it give the clues, so read them first.
explain: «Scientists found that a dandelion seed's parachute makes a little ring of swirling air above it that holds it up longer.» The air is moving round and round in circles. «Swirling» is the -ing form of the verb, so the air is still moving.
explain: Use the swap test. Put «move round and round quickly in circles» into the sentence: «The starlings move round and round quickly in circles over the roofs at dusk» still makes sense, so that is the meaning.
fact: To swirl means to move round and round quickly in circles, like water going down a plughole.
fact: To swirl something means to make it turn round, like swirling paint in water.
fact: A swirl is a twisting, circling shape or movement, like «a swirl of cream».
fact: «Swirl» is a verb (swirl, swirls, swirled, swirling) and a noun (a swirl, swirls).
fact: «Swirl around» is a common phrase, as in «Snow began to swirl around the castle».
exercise: «Snow began to swirl around the castle.» What does swirl mean here? | To stay perfectly still on the ground | *To move round and round quickly in circles | To melt slowly into water | To fall straight down in a line
exercise: In «a swirl of cream», what word class is swirl? | An adjective, a describing word | *A noun, a thing | A verb, an action word | A preposition, a word of place
exercise: «Each bird gets a little lift from the air swirling off the wing tips.» Which word could replace swirling and keep the same meaning? | *turning round in circles | sinking slowly | sitting still | singing loudly
test: «Mist swirls around the castle.» Which word means the same as swirls? | slides straight down | stays very still | *circles round and round | sparkles brightly
test: «Tom swirled the paint in the water.» What does swirled mean here? | painted a straight line | poured the water away | dried the paint quickly | *made the paint turn round in circles
exam: Which sentence uses swirl as a noun? | The leaves swirl in the wind. | *There was a swirl of mist over the lake. | Water swirls down the plughole. | Starlings swirl over the roofs at dusk.
